# `M154g` / `C76` — the known-answer plant for `@tags`. **This file is meant to pass**, in every
# selection the grader runs it under.
#
# Tags are everywhere in this suite — every file here carries them — and a tag that selected nothing
# would leave all of it green, because the suite's ordinary runs are unfiltered. Presence is the
# purest case of `D739`: the construct is used constantly and its *effect* is never observed.
#
# The effect is a partition, so the plant is built as one. Three tests, three labels, three
# tag-sets, and the grader runs the file four times and compares what the server received:
#
#   (no flag)                   alpha beta both     nothing is filtered out by default
#   --tag c76alpha              alpha       both    and beta is ABSENT — the discriminating half
#   --tag c76beta                     beta  both    the complement, so neither run is a coincidence
#   --tag c76alpha,c76beta      alpha beta both     OR across a comma-separated list
#
# The third run matters as much as the second: a `--tag` that silently matched everything passes the
# first and fourth, and a `--tag` that matched only the first-listed tag of each test would pass the
# second while failing the third.
#
# `c76both` carries both tags and is expected in all four, which is what makes this a partition
# rather than three disjoint filters — `--tag` selects a test carrying *any* listed tag, never only
# the ones tagged exclusively.

# Reset here rather than in the grader, so each of the four runs starts from zero on its own and
# the counts the grader reads are always that run's alone. `before file` is not tag-filtered — it
# belongs to the file, not to a test — so it runs under every selection below.
before file
  api POST /lifecycle/reset
  expect status equals 200

@constructs @c76alpha
test "carries c76alpha only"
  api POST /lifecycle/mark body { label: "c76alpha" }
  expect status equals 200

@constructs @c76beta
test "carries c76beta only"
  api POST /lifecycle/mark body { label: "c76beta" }
  expect status equals 200

@constructs @c76alpha @c76beta
test "carries both, so every selection above reaches it"
  api POST /lifecycle/mark body { label: "c76both" }
  expect status equals 200
